<title>UK: London Tea Auction price indications.</title>
<headline>London Tea Auction price indications.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>At today's London landed Tea Auction of 5,400 packages of 53.50 kgs, including 1,200 offshore, price indications in pence a kilo compared to the last sale and the corresponding week last year.</p>
<p>    Best available  135   (149 and 130)</p>
<p>    Good		unq   (146 and 120)</p>
<p>    Good Medium     128   (133 and 112)</p>
<p>    Medium	    120   (125 and 105)</p>
<p>    Low Medium	 88    (88 and  82)</p>
<p>The highest price paid was 135 pence for a Ceylon BOP.</p>
</text>
